1
00:00:00,433 --> 00:00:02,467
Are you a SMART fella...

2
00:00:02,467 --> 00:00:04,533
or a FART smella?

3
00:00:04,533 --> 00:00:06,800
Let's find OUT!

4
00:00:07,733 --> 00:00:10,433
Question one! Which one does NOT

5
00:00:10,433 --> 00:00:13,467
belong? Robin... sparrow...

6
00:00:13,467 --> 00:00:16,333
salmon... eagle. Is it A,

7
00:00:16,333 --> 00:00:19,133
robin... B, sparrow...

8
00:00:19,267 --> 00:00:21,467
C, salmon... or D,

9
00:00:21,467 --> 00:00:24,167
eagle? Five seconds, go!

10
00:00:29,767 --> 00:00:32,300
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

11
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:34,200
The answer is...

12
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:37,000
C, salmon! A robin,

13
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,200
a sparrow, and an eagle all

14
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:41,333
soar through the sky as birds.

15
00:00:41,333 --> 00:00:42,367
But a salmon?

16
00:00:42,367 --> 00:00:43,800
That one swims.

17
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:45,367
It's a fish!

18
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:48,833
Question two, a number series!

19
00:00:48,833 --> 00:00:50,967
Three, six, twelve,

20
00:00:50,967 --> 00:00:53,000
twenty-four, and then...

21
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:54,367
what comes next?

22
00:00:54,367 --> 00:00:56,700
A, thirty-six... B,

23
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:59,100
forty-eight... C, thirty...

24
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:01,000
or D, forty-two?

25
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,533
Five seconds!

26
00:01:08,100 --> 00:01:10,633
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

27
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,633
It's... B, forty-eight!

28
00:01:13,633 --> 00:01:15,633
Each number simply doubles:

29
00:01:15,633 --> 00:01:17,833
three, six, twelve,

30
00:01:17,833 --> 00:01:19,733
twenty-four... and twenty-four

31
00:01:19,733 --> 00:01:22,333
times two is forty-eight!

32
00:01:23,167 --> 00:01:25,900
Question three, a picture puzzle!

33
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:28,000
An empty circle becomes a filled-in

34
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:31,300
circle. So an empty square becomes...

35
00:01:31,300 --> 00:01:33,033
which one? A,

36
00:01:33,033 --> 00:01:34,400
a filled square...

37
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:36,700
B, an empty square...

38
00:01:36,767 --> 00:01:38,633
C, a filled circle...

39
00:01:38,633 --> 00:01:41,400
or D, a filled triangle?

40
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:42,833
Six seconds!

41
00:01:49,333 --> 00:01:51,867
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

42
00:01:52,233 --> 00:01:53,633
The answer is...

43
00:01:53,633 --> 00:01:55,867
A, a filled square!

44
00:01:55,867 --> 00:01:57,433
The rule is simple:

45
00:01:57,433 --> 00:01:59,033
the shape gets colored in,

46
00:01:59,033 --> 00:02:01,400
but stays the very same shape.

47
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:04,733
Empty square becomes filled square!

48
00:02:05,633 --> 00:02:08,367
Question four, a word analogy!

49
00:02:08,367 --> 00:02:10,133
Giant is to tiny,

50
00:02:10,133 --> 00:02:12,133
as wide is to...

51
00:02:12,133 --> 00:02:14,467
what? A, narrow...

52
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:16,567
B, tall... C,

53
00:02:16,567 --> 00:02:18,333
long... or D,

54
00:02:18,333 --> 00:02:21,200
big? Five seconds, go!

55
00:02:26,767 --> 00:02:29,300
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

56
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:32,100
It's... A, narrow!

57
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:34,667
Giant and tiny are opposites,

58
00:02:34,667 --> 00:02:36,567
so just flip 'wide' to its

59
00:02:36,567 --> 00:02:39,300
opposite, and that's narrow!

60
00:02:40,267 --> 00:02:43,267
Question five, another number series!

61
00:02:43,267 --> 00:02:45,467
One hundred, ninety-two,

62
00:02:45,467 --> 00:02:48,933
eighty-four, seventy-six, and then...

63
00:02:48,933 --> 00:02:51,267
what? A, seventy...

64
00:02:51,267 --> 00:02:53,700
B, sixty-eight... C,

65
00:02:53,700 --> 00:02:55,900
sixty-six... or D,

66
00:02:55,900 --> 00:02:58,667
seventy-two? Five seconds!

67
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:06,733
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

68
00:03:07,033 --> 00:03:08,400
The answer is...

69
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:11,400
B, sixty-eight! Every step drops

70
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:13,733
by eight, and seventy-six minus

71
00:03:13,733 --> 00:03:15,600
eight is sixty-eight!

72
00:03:16,533 --> 00:03:19,267
Question six, a word analogy!

73
00:03:19,267 --> 00:03:20,667
Ocean is to puddle,

74
00:03:20,667 --> 00:03:22,567
as mountain is to...

75
00:03:22,567 --> 00:03:25,000
what? A, valley...

76
00:03:25,167 --> 00:03:27,400
B, hill... C,

77
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:29,033
river... or D,

78
00:03:29,033 --> 00:03:31,267
rock? Five seconds!

79
00:03:36,767 --> 00:03:39,300
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

80
00:03:39,667 --> 00:03:42,300
It's... B, hill!

81
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:44,133
An ocean shrinks down to a

82
00:03:44,133 --> 00:03:46,467
tiny puddle, so a mountain shrinks

83
00:03:46,467 --> 00:03:48,200
down to a little hill.

84
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:50,700
Same thing, pocket-sized!

85
00:03:51,667 --> 00:03:54,600
Question seven, and this one is

86
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:57,133
tricky! Two, six,

87
00:03:57,133 --> 00:03:59,867
twelve, twenty, thirty,

88
00:03:59,867 --> 00:04:02,633
and then... what comes next?

89
00:04:02,667 --> 00:04:05,233
A, thirty-six... B,

90
00:04:05,233 --> 00:04:08,100
forty... C, forty-two...

91
00:04:08,100 --> 00:04:10,433
or D, forty-four?

92
00:04:10,433 --> 00:04:12,600
Seven seconds on the clock!

93
00:04:20,133 --> 00:04:22,667
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

94
00:04:23,033 --> 00:04:24,367
The answer is...

95
00:04:24,367 --> 00:04:27,333
C, forty-two! Look at the jumps:

96
00:04:27,333 --> 00:04:29,333
plus four, plus six,

97
00:04:29,333 --> 00:04:31,333
plus eight, plus ten.

98
00:04:31,333 --> 00:04:33,500
The next jump is plus twelve,

99
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:36,633
and thirty plus twelve is forty-two!

100
00:04:37,633 --> 00:04:40,100
Question eight, a word analogy!

101
00:04:40,100 --> 00:04:41,767
Painter is to brush,

102
00:04:41,767 --> 00:04:43,900
as carpenter is to...

103
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:46,033
what? A, hammer...

104
00:04:46,033 --> 00:04:48,467
B, wood... C,

105
00:04:48,467 --> 00:04:50,333
house... or D,

106
00:04:50,333 --> 00:04:52,333
nail? Five seconds!

107
00:04:57,833 --> 00:05:00,367
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

108
00:05:00,733 --> 00:05:02,567
It's... A, hammer!

109
00:05:02,567 --> 00:05:04,700
A painter's tool is a brush,

110
00:05:04,700 --> 00:05:06,433
and a carpenter's tool is a

111
00:05:06,433 --> 00:05:09,333
hammer. Wood is just the material,

112
00:05:09,333 --> 00:05:11,900
and a house is what you build!

113
00:05:12,833 --> 00:05:15,867
Question nine, a number series!

114
00:05:15,867 --> 00:05:17,833
One, one, two,

115
00:05:17,833 --> 00:05:19,767
three, five, eight,

116
00:05:19,767 --> 00:05:22,167
and then... what comes next?

117
00:05:22,167 --> 00:05:24,033
A, eleven... B,

118
00:05:24,033 --> 00:05:26,467
thirteen... C, twelve...

119
00:05:26,467 --> 00:05:28,533
or D, sixteen?

120
00:05:28,533 --> 00:05:30,167
Seven seconds!

121
00:05:37,733 --> 00:05:40,267
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

122
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:42,133
The answer is...

123
00:05:42,133 --> 00:05:44,800
B, thirteen! Add the two numbers

124
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:47,000
before it: five plus eight is

125
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:50,633
thirteen. That's the famous Fibonacci pattern!

126
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:54,067
Question ten! Which one does NOT

127
00:05:54,067 --> 00:05:57,067
belong? Add... subtract...

128
00:05:57,067 --> 00:06:00,033
multiply... number. A,

129
00:06:00,033 --> 00:06:02,833
add... B, subtract...

130
00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:05,833
C, multiply... or D,

131
00:06:05,833 --> 00:06:08,467
number? Five seconds!

132
00:06:14,133 --> 00:06:16,667
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

133
00:06:17,033 --> 00:06:19,567
It's... D, number!

134
00:06:19,567 --> 00:06:22,233
Add, subtract, and multiply are

135
00:06:22,233 --> 00:06:23,533
all things you do.

136
00:06:23,533 --> 00:06:24,500
But a number?

137
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:26,800
That's the thing you do them to!

138
00:06:27,700 --> 00:06:30,533
Question eleven, a shape puzzle!

139
00:06:30,533 --> 00:06:31,733
Watch them grow,

140
00:06:31,733 --> 00:06:34,033
gaining one side each step:

141
00:06:34,033 --> 00:06:36,133
a triangle, then a square,

142
00:06:36,133 --> 00:06:37,800
then a pentagon.

143
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:39,733
Which shape comes next?

144
00:06:39,733 --> 00:06:41,033
A, a circle...

145
00:06:41,033 --> 00:06:43,233
B, a hexagon...

146
00:06:43,233 --> 00:06:44,667
C, a square...

147
00:06:44,667 --> 00:06:47,033
or D, an octagon?

148
00:06:47,033 --> 00:06:48,633
Seven seconds!

149
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:58,733
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

150
00:06:59,067 --> 00:07:00,533
The answer is...

151
00:07:00,533 --> 00:07:03,533
B, hexagon! Count the sides:

152
00:07:03,533 --> 00:07:06,133
triangle three, square four,

153
00:07:06,133 --> 00:07:08,833
pentagon five... so next up is

154
00:07:08,833 --> 00:07:11,367
the six-sided hexagon!

155
00:07:12,267 --> 00:07:15,100
Question twelve, fill in the blank!

156
00:07:15,100 --> 00:07:17,000
The bridge was too weak to

157
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,400
hold the heavy truck,

158
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:20,600
so workers had to blank it

159
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:22,267
before opening the road.

160
00:07:22,267 --> 00:07:24,500
A, decorate... B,

161
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:27,600
reinforce... C, rename...

162
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:29,533
or D, measure?

163
00:07:29,533 --> 00:07:30,867
Six seconds!

164
00:07:37,367 --> 00:07:39,900
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

165
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:43,067
It's... B, reinforce!

166
00:07:43,067 --> 00:07:44,667
Too weak means you have to

167
00:07:44,667 --> 00:07:45,800
make it stronger,

168
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:48,100
and reinforce is the only word

169
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:49,900
that fixes the problem!

170
00:07:50,767 --> 00:07:53,500
Question thirteen, a picture puzzle!

171
00:07:53,500 --> 00:07:55,467
A dot marches clockwise around

172
00:07:55,467 --> 00:07:57,367
a square: top-left,

173
00:07:57,367 --> 00:07:59,633
top-right, bottom-right... where

174
00:07:59,633 --> 00:08:01,000
does it jump next?

175
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:03,167
A, top-left... B,

176
00:08:03,167 --> 00:08:05,833
bottom-left... C, top-right...

177
00:08:05,833 --> 00:08:07,767
or D, the center?

178
00:08:07,767 --> 00:08:09,100
Seven seconds!

179
00:08:16,633 --> 00:08:19,167
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

180
00:08:19,467 --> 00:08:20,833
The answer is...

181
00:08:20,833 --> 00:08:24,367
B, bottom-left! The dot steps clockwise,

182
00:08:24,367 --> 00:08:25,433
corner to corner,

183
00:08:25,433 --> 00:08:27,100
and right after bottom-right,

184
00:08:27,100 --> 00:08:29,500
the next corner is bottom-left!

185
00:08:30,333 --> 00:08:33,433
Question fourteen, a number analogy!

186
00:08:33,433 --> 00:08:34,700
Two makes five,

187
00:08:34,700 --> 00:08:35,967
three makes seven,

188
00:08:35,967 --> 00:08:37,267
four makes nine,

189
00:08:37,267 --> 00:08:38,900
so five makes...

190
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:40,933
what? A, ten...

191
00:08:40,967 --> 00:08:42,833
B, eleven... C,

192
00:08:42,833 --> 00:08:44,467
twelve... or D,

193
00:08:44,467 --> 00:08:46,967
thirteen? Six seconds!

194
00:08:53,467 --> 00:08:56,000
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

195
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:58,833
It's... B, eleven!

196
00:08:58,833 --> 00:09:00,300
Each number is doubled,

197
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:01,733
then add one.

198
00:09:01,733 --> 00:09:03,733
Five times two is ten,

199
00:09:03,733 --> 00:09:06,033
plus one is eleven!

200
00:09:07,133 --> 00:09:09,467
Last one, question fifteen,

201
00:09:09,467 --> 00:09:10,833
a number puzzle,

202
00:09:10,833 --> 00:09:12,267
and it's sneaky!

203
00:09:12,267 --> 00:09:14,667
If four plus five makes twenty,

204
00:09:14,667 --> 00:09:17,267
three plus six makes eighteen,

205
00:09:17,267 --> 00:09:19,967
and two plus seven makes fourteen...

206
00:09:19,967 --> 00:09:22,333
then five plus four makes...

207
00:09:22,333 --> 00:09:24,767
what? A, nine...

208
00:09:24,767 --> 00:09:27,067
B, eighteen... C,

209
00:09:27,067 --> 00:09:28,733
twenty... or D,

210
00:09:28,733 --> 00:09:31,633
twenty-five? Seven seconds!

211
00:09:39,233 --> 00:09:41,767
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

212
00:09:42,067 --> 00:09:43,533
The answer is...

213
00:09:43,533 --> 00:09:45,967
C, twenty! Here's the trick:

214
00:09:45,967 --> 00:09:49,267
that plus sign secretly means multiply.

215
00:09:49,267 --> 00:09:51,067
Four times five is twenty,

216
00:09:51,067 --> 00:09:54,167
so five times four is twenty too!

217
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:58,133
So, are you smart or fart?

218
00:09:58,133 --> 00:09:59,900
Count up your correct answers to

219
00:09:59,900 --> 00:10:01,533
find your rank!

220
00:10:02,400 --> 00:10:04,000
So, how did you do?

221
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,500
Comment your score below,

222
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:07,333
and subscribe for more!
